## Order of operations

{% if groups_to_create -%}
**The route66_ldap_groups MR must be merged and applied BEFORE the route66 MR.**
The `keycloak_client_roles` module reads each AD group via `data "keycloak_group"`. If the
group doesn't exist in Keycloak yet, the route66 apply will fail.

LDAP→Keycloak sync runs every 15 minutes (`changed_sync_period = 900`). After the
`route66_ldap_groups` apply succeeds, wait for the sync (or ask DevOps to trigger
it manually) before merging the route66 MR.

1. Merge & apply: `route66_ldap_groups` MR
2. Wait for AD→Keycloak sync (≤15 min)
3. Merge & apply: `route66` MR
{% else -%}
1. Merge & apply: `route66` MR
{% endif %}

## DevOps checklist (after each terraform apply)

- [ ] `route66_ldap_groups` pipeline `deploy` job is green {{"" if groups_to_create else "(N/A — no LDAP changes)"}}
- [ ] AD→Keycloak sync has propagated the new groups (visible under realm Groups in Keycloak Admin UI) {{"" if groups_to_create else "(N/A)"}}
- [ ] `route66` pipeline `deploy` job is green
{%- if client_type == "confidential" or auth_scenario == "client_credentials" %}
- [ ] Read the auto-generated `CLIENT_SECRET` from Keycloak Admin UI:
      `Clients → {{app_name}} → Credentials → Client secret`
- [ ] Deliver `CLIENT_SECRET` to the developer through the corporate secret-sharing channel.
      **Do NOT** paste it into git, GitLab MR comments, Slack, Mattermost, email, or any
      ticket system. Use the company Vault / password-share tool only.
{%- endif %}

